# Generated per point by mc/make_param_card.py.
# Example from the repository root:
#
#   python3 mc/make_param_card.py \
#     --out mc/cards/belle2/param_card.dat \
#     --m-a 1.0 \
#     --g-agg 1e-4 \
#     --fa 1000 \
#     --width-mode stable
#
# The UFO-native scan handles are fa, KB, and KW. The writer converts
# physical g_agg to KB+KW using the Gate-1 production normalization:
#
#   g_agg = alpha_em * (KB + KW) / (sqrt(2) * pi * fa)
#
# By default, --g-agg uses the KB/KW split that cancels the tree-level
# gamma-Z-ALP coupling. Use --kb-fraction only when intentionally scanning a
# different electroweak-basis split.
